/E (The draw_grid function is responsible for displaying a grid on a GUI canvas \(most likely using Tkinter\). It visually represents the internal state of a 2D grid \(self.grid\) by drawing colored rectangles, where each color corresponds to the value in a specific cell. First, it clears any existing drawings on the canvas using self.canvas.delete\("all"\) to make sure the grid is redrawn cleanly every time this function is called.)
/Pg 16 0 R
