/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The get_neighbors_color_counts method starts by creating a 2D list called visited to track which grid cells have already been checked. It initializes a queue with the starting cell \(0, 0\), sets the start_color as the color of that cell, and marks it as visited. It also creates a color_count list initialized with zeros, where each index corresponds to a color and counts how many times it appears around the flood area. Then it enters a while loop that runs as long as there are cells in the queue. In each iteration, it removes the first cell from the queue and checks its four neighbors \(up, down, left, right\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
