/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (If the new color is the same as the original, it returns immediately to avoid unnecessary work. It initializes a visited set to track visited cells and a stack with the starting position for DFS traversal. Inside the while loop, it pops a cell from the stack and checks if it has already been visited; if so, it skips it. If not, it marks the cell as visited, changes its color to new_color, and then checks its four neighbors \(up, down, left, right\). For each valid neighbor inside the grid boundaries that has the original color, it adds that cell to the stack for further processing. This continues until all connected cells with the same original color are filled.)
/E (If the new color is the same as the original, it returns immediately to avoid unnecessary work. It initializes a visited set to track visited cells and a stack with the starting position for DFS traversal. Inside the while loop, it pops a cell from the stack and checks if it has already been visited; if so, it skips it. If not, it marks the cell as visited, changes its color to new_color, and then checks its four neighbors \(up, down, left, right\). For each valid neighbor inside the grid boundaries that has the original color, it adds that cell to the stack for further processing. This continues until all connected cells with the same original color are filled.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
